# ThreadSanitizer suppressions for test_concurrency (.github/workflows/tsan.yml).
#
# Rule: suppress only races inside third-party code we do not build with
# -fsanitize=thread; a race in libembedding's own code is a bug to fix, never
# an entry here. Each entry needs a comment saying what it is and since when.
#
# ONNX Runtime is a prebuilt, uninstrumented binary: TSan sees its thread-pool
# and Eigen spin-waits without the synchronisation (futex, custom atomics) it
# cannot model, and reports races that are not ones. Everything reached from
# the ORT library is ignored; our own frames that call into it stay checked.
called_from_lib:libonnxruntime.so*

# glibc 2.39 (ubuntu-24.04 runner) releases an internal lock during exit()
# that TSan (clang 18) did not see taken: "unlock of an unlocked mutex" whose
# whole stack is pthread_mutex_unlock called from libc.so.6, after every check
# of test_concurrency has passed. Not our code. Added 2026-11-18.
mutex:libc.so.6
